# Program display timezone (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-08-16): times use the program default
timezone set by the super administrator. The zone is always shown on
the time string. UTC and GMT as the silent default are unneeded
complexity. Storage stays a modern instant so calculations stay
correct in every zone.

## The rule

> **Every operator-facing clock uses `DISPLAY_TIMEZONE` (IANA). Empty
> means host or client local time — never silent UTC. The zone
> abbreviation or `UTC±HH:MM` offset is always part of the string.
> Instants on the wire and in the database stay RFC 3339 / ISO 8601
> so arithmetic is timezone-correct. Logs in `local` mode use the
> same program zone (or host local) and always include the offset.**

## Configuration

| Surface | Detail |
| --- | --- |
| Manifest | `DISPLAY_TIMEZONE` in `pim-offline-server/app-config.toml` |
| Super-admin UI | Settings → General → Program time zone |
| API | `GET`/`PUT /api/admin/display-timezone` |
| Session | IAM session JSON also returns `display_timezone*` |
| Logs | `LOG_TIME_ZONE=local` (default) calls `display_time::format_now_local()` |

Empty `DISPLAY_TIMEZONE` follows the host (server logs) or the
browser (SPA) local zone. Super administrators may set an IANA id
such as `America/Los_Angeles`. `gmt` remains an explicit log-mode
opt-in, not the product default.

## Required display

Example: `2026-08-15 10:23:00 PDT (UTC-07:00)`

- SPA: `formatAppDateTime` / `useDisplayTime()` /
  `DisplayTimeProvider` (sets the shared current zone so older
  `formatUtc` helpers follow it)
- Server: `crate::display_time::format_instant`

## Forbidden

- Rendering `toISOString()` or `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM UTC` as operator
  chrome
- Defaulting a new clock to UTC/GMT because “that is simpler”
- Storing wall-clock-without-offset as the source of truth
- Inventing a product env var for the zone
  ([`no-environment-variables.mdc`](no-environment-variables.mdc))
- Lab hostnames or “BEAVIS2 local” in the Settings helper
  ([`no-lab-config-in-operator-ui.mdc`](no-lab-config-in-operator-ui.mdc))

## Origin

